    {
      "id": "U4U-READ-1",
      "paper": "review",
      "title": "Ken's First Job",
      "text": "Ken finished his education last summer, but for months he was out of work. He did not boast about himself. He was honest and worked hard every day. One morning, a chain store called him for an interview. Ken was about to leave home when his mother gave him a gold pen for luck. At the interview, the interviewer asked many questions. Ken kept his answers in order and did not talk too much, because too much talk can do harm. His honesty soon gained the manager's trust. \"Perhaps you are the one we need,\" the manager said. The store would provide good training and supply a free lunch every day. Ken felt no more pain in his stomach. It was a great honor to get his first real job."
    }
  ],
